  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 336 AM EDT Sat Jul 4 2026\n\nDaily rain chances and slightly above normal temperatures are \nforecast in the long term period. A passing trough Sunday into \nMonday bringing decent rain chances (30-60%) back to the area, most \nfavored in the north. From here, high pressure remains situated over \nthe western Atlantic which may eventually extend further east \ntowards the latter half of the week. This pattern keeps above normal \nmoisture over the area aiding in the daily thunderstorm chances \nwhich are highest each afternoon and evening. Widespread \ntemperatures in the mid and upper 90s are expected Sunday except in \nthe mountains, then temperatures drop a few degrees Monday and \nremain relatively steady for the rest of the period. Heat indices \ncontinue to range from the upper 90s to around 105 degrees.",
